    summary: "Joshua 9 records how Israel made a treaty with the Gibeonites without asking the Lord. First Samuel 13:8-14 shows Saul offering a sacrifice in fear and impatience. Proverbs 19:2 warns that hurrying makes one miss the way, and Proverbs 29:20 warns about hasty words. This lesson gives practical tools for pressure decisions: pause, pray, ask, sleep on it and decide with clear principles.",
    scripture: ["Joshua 9:3-16", "Proverbs 19:2"], more: ["1 Samuel 13:8-14", "Proverbs 29:20", "Isaiah 28:16"], memory: "Proverbs 19:2",
